    // For the purpose of this example, we'll assume the FFT is computed
    // and stored in a complex array
    // float complex X[kN];
    // ... compute FFT ...

    // Compute the spectral derivative D[k] = i * w(k) * X[k]
    // float complex D[kN];
    // ... compute D[k] ...

    // Compute the inverse FFT of D[k] to get dx[b]
